---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import TimeLineElement from "../components/cv/TimeLine.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Resume" sideBarActiveItemID="background">
  <div class="mb-5">
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold">Profile</div>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-10 text-justify">
    Computer Engineering senior at Johns Hopkins University (graduating May
    2027) focused on RTL design, design verification, and FPGA/ASIC
    engineering. Experience spans FPGA protocol design in VHDL, low-level
    C/C++ systems work, and student leadership as Co-President of the JHU
    chapter of the National Society of Black Engineers. U.S. Citizen.
    <br /><br />
    <span class="font-bold">Looking for:</span> full-time roles in RTL design,
    design verification, FPGA, and embedded engineering, starting after I
    graduate in May 2027. I'm open to relocating and to other opportunities for
    hands-on hardware experience.
  </div>

  <div class="bg-base-200 p-6 rounded-lg my-8">
    <blockquote class="italic text-lg mb-4">
      "Morgan successfully navigated the challenge with distinction... his
      continued learning outside the classroom speaks volumes about his grit,
      determination, and passion for self-directed learning. I firmly believe
      Morgan will prove an asset to any team."
      <footer class="mt-2 text-sm not-italic font-semibold text-right">
        — Brennon Brimhall, Instructor & Researcher, Johns Hopkins University
      </footer>
    </blockquote>
    <div class="flex justify-center">
      <a href="/letter.pdf" target="_blank" class="btn btn-primary"
        >Read Full Recommendation Letter</a
      >
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-5">
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold">Education</div>
  </div>

  <div class="time-line-container grid gap-4 mb-10">
    <TimeLineElement
      title="B.S. Computer Engineering"
      subtitle="Expected May 2027 at Johns Hopkins University, Baltimore, USA"
    >
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 mt-2">
        <span class="badge badge-outline">FPGA Lab</span>
        <span class="badge badge-outline">Computer System Fundamentals</span>
        <span class="badge badge-outline">Signals & Systems</span>
        <span class="badge badge-outline">Mastering Electronics</span>
        <span class="badge badge-outline">Robots, Sensors & Actuators</span>
        <span class="badge badge-outline">Computer Vision</span>
        <span class="badge badge-outline">Data Structures</span>
      </div>
    </TimeLineElement>
    <TimeLineElement
      title="Engineering Math, Marketing Fundamentals for Media"
      subtitle="Jan 2022 to Jun 2023 at Lethbridge College (online)"
    />
    <TimeLineElement
      title="Introduction to Business Management"
      subtitle="Sep 2021 to Dec 2021 at Southern Alberta Institute of Technology (online)"
    />
  </div>

  <div class="mb-5">
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold">Experience</div>
  </div>

  <div class="time-line-container mb-10">
    <TimeLineElement
      title="Software Engineering Intern (Edge Software Optimization) at Morgate Solutions"
      subtitle="Jun 2026 to Aug 2026"
    >
      • Containerized C/C++ parsers with Docker for Linux edge gateways,
      optimizing memory use to fit 512 MB device limits<br />
      • Emulated network jitter and profiled CPU usage to find and prevent
      buffer overflows in high-frequency data streams
    </TimeLineElement>
    <TimeLineElement
      title="Data Science Researcher at #iVoted Impact Concerts, SNF Agora Institute"
      subtitle="May 2025 to May 2026"
    >
      • Processed music-listener and voter-demographic data from
      RedistrictingDataHub & Geocorr APIs<br />
      • Automated weekly ETL workflows with Python and the Google Sheets API<br
      />
      • Maintained dashboards that projected concert-driven voter registrations
    </TimeLineElement>
    <TimeLineElement
      title="Software Engineering Intern (Low-Level Data & Protocol Bridging) at Morgate Solutions"
      subtitle="Jun 2024 to Aug 2024"
    >
      • Developed C extraction tools using struct packing and bitwise
      operations to decode 50+ GB of binary telemetry<br />
      • Managed struct byte alignment and endianness; built a Python test
      harness to validate parser output
    </TimeLineElement>
    <TimeLineElement
      title="Robotics Designer at VEX Robotics"
      subtitle="Nov 2019 to Mar 2023"
    >
      • Designed & programmed competition robots in C++ / Python<br />
      • Integrated sensors, tuned motor controllers, and produced CAD for
      3-D-printed parts<br />
      • Diagnosed mechanical/electrical issues and iterated designs
    </TimeLineElement>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-5">
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold">Leadership</div>
  </div>

  <div class="time-line-container mb-10">
    <TimeLineElement
      title="Co-President at National Society of Black Engineers, JHU Chapter"
      subtitle="Sep 2023 to Present (previously Vice President and Finance Chair)"
    >
      • Secured sponsorships from Medtronic, Visa, and Jane Street; hosted
      events with Medtronic and Shift Alt Her<br />
      • Grew reach through events with JHU's Life Design Lab and Pava Center and
      collaborations with five student organizations, including SHPE and BMES<br
      />
      • Building the chapter website; grew outreach on Instagram and LinkedIn
      and started alumni LinkedIn and WhatsApp groups<br />
      • Delegate committee work, run fundraisers and logistics, and fund member
      travel to regional and national conferences<br />
      • As Finance Chair, managed a $9K annual budget and secured $3.5K through
      fundraising and corporate sponsorships
    </TimeLineElement>
    <TimeLineElement
      title="Fundraising Chair at HopThon, JHU Dance Marathon"
      subtitle="Fall 2025 to Spring 2026"
    />
    <TimeLineElement
      title="Philanthropy Chair at Alpha Epsilon Pi"
      subtitle="Spring 2025"
    />
  </div>

  <div class="mb-5">
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold">Skills</div>
  </div>

  <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 mx-6">
    <span class="badge badge-outline">VHDL</span>
    <span class="badge badge-outline">Verilog</span>
    <span class="badge badge-outline">Verilator</span>
    <span class="badge badge-outline">Xilinx Vivado (Synthesis, Place and Route)</span>
    <span class="badge badge-outline">Self-Checking Testbenches</span>
    <span class="badge badge-outline">LTSpice</span>
    <span class="badge badge-outline">Oscilloscope</span>
    <span class="badge badge-outline">Multimeter</span>
    <span class="badge badge-outline">C/C++</span>
    <span class="badge badge-outline">Arduino</span>
    <span class="badge badge-outline">Python (NumPy, Pandas, Matplotlib)</span>
    <span class="badge badge-outline">MATLAB</span>
    <span class="badge badge-outline">Bash</span>
    <span class="badge badge-outline">Linux (Ubuntu)</span>
    <span class="badge badge-outline">Git</span>
    <span class="badge badge-outline">Docker</span>
    <span class="badge badge-outline">GenAI Tools (Claude, Gemini, Cursor)</span>
    <span class="badge badge-outline">SystemVerilog (Learning)</span>
    <span class="badge badge-outline">SystemC (Learning)</span>
  </div>

  <div class="mt-8 bg-base-200 p-4 rounded-lg mx-6">
    <h4 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2">Foundational Concepts</h4>
    <p class="text-lg">
      Digital design and RTL, FSM design, clock domain crossing (CDC) with
      two-flop synchronizers for asynchronous inputs, UART, I²C and SPI protocol
      implementation, open-drain I/O, microcontroller firmware, circuit
      analysis, analog and digital (continuous- and discrete-time) signals,
      cache and memory hierarchy, binary data formats (struct packing,
      endianness), and basic x86-64 assembly.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
